# hui 214+P grenade (arcing projectile -> ground explosion) on a 2P
# DUMMY (14z-70). The comparable twin of 83_hui_fx.rpl, which cannot be
# used for a cross-leg comparison at all:
#
#   83 is 1P-vs-CPU (sys=C1, sys=S1, no C2/S2). vsav2 and vsavjw pick a
#   DIFFERENT CPU opponent AND a different stage, so the two legs are
#   two unrelated matches — at f3436 native is at range with the
#   explosion on screen while ours has Felicia point-blank and the
#   projectile never travels. A frame-matched sprite diff on 83 compares
#   different matches and will produce confident nonsense (it did:
#   "101 codes, zero overlap", discarded 14z-70).
#
# BOTH SIDES ARE POKED. P1 = Huitzil (native 0x10 on both games), P2 =
# Victor (0x03 on vsav AND vsav2). The cursor path lands on different
# characters on the two wheels, so poking only P1 leaves P2 divergent
# and the comparison is worthless again — the HANDOFF rule for any
# measurement that compares sprite lists.
#
# Early-window pokes ONLY (1400-1500): late pokes leak into the 2P
# commit/load path (the replay-80 rule).
# POKES="1400:ff8782:10;1450:ff8782:10;1500:ff8782:10;1400:ff8b82:03;1450:ff8b82:03;1500:ff8b82:03"
#
# TWO SPACED ATTEMPTS: the seq-D dispatch thunk shifts frame-pinned
# inputs by a few cycles, so any single attempt can be eaten. Either
# landing is enough to photograph the explosion.
300-305 sys=C1
420-425 sys=C2
800-803 sys=S1
940-943 sys=S2
1100-1102 p2=R
1160-1162 p2=R
1300-1302 p1=1
1360-1362 p2=1
# 214MP #1 — quarter-circle back + medium punch, P1 at the 2P start range
3380-3382 p1=D
3383-3385 p1=DL
3386-3388 p1=L2
# 214MP #2
3680-3682 p1=D
3683-3685 p1=DL
3686-3688 p1=L2
3900 wait
